      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">35 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Pattern primer</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tries</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Asked by Amazon, Uber, Google, DoorDash, Snowflake, Docusign</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Tries</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">A trie is a tree whose edges are letters (or bits), so every word that shares a prefix shares a path. Insert, search and prefix checks cost O(length of the word), independent of how many words you store, and one walk down the trie can test thousands of words at once: that is what makes Word Search II, autocomplete and max-XOR fast.</p>\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Go deeper:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-string-matching\">String matching: KMP, Z-function, rolling hash</a>.</p>\n"
  },
